{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he shall be sold for his theft.</b> For were it not for this, most of the poor of the nation would be thieves — for if the stolen item is lost or consumed, there is no saying 'restore it,' since the man has no means to pay, and so the land would be filled with violence."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Reading מִבְּלִי אֵין as 'since there is not [wherewithal] in the man's hand to pay'; the phrase is slightly awkward in the Hebrew and may reflect a textual corruption."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:43.669596053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}